{%- comment -%}
  PawLunova: what this bed actually is, in four or five ticks, directly under the price.

  The shopper's first question on a bed page is "does it fit my dog and is it the
  right kind" — and today that answer is buried in the description, four scrolls
  down, behind a size table. These ticks lift the four or five facts that decide
  it up to the buy box.

  Every line comes from the product's OWN data and renders only when that data
  exists. Nothing is inferred, averaged or borrowed from a similar bed: a wrong
  spec on a dog bed is a return, and blank is honest where unknown. A product
  with no populated fields renders nothing at all rather than a stub.

  Order is deliberate, most-decisive first:
    1. which dog it takes      (custom.max_dog_weight, else parsed from the title)
    2. what is inside it       (custom.core_type + custom.foam_depth)
    3. the cover               (custom.cover_type)
    4. getting in              (custom.low_entry, else custom.shape)
    5. how long it is backed   (custom.foam_guarantee + the guarantee setting)

  Capped at `max` ticks (default 5) so the buy box never grows a wall of text.

  Usage, from the product template under the price:
    {% render 'pln-spec-ticks', product: product %}
    {% render 'pln-spec-ticks', product: product, max: 4 %}

  Styles: assets/pln-pdp.css, section "spec ticks".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign limit = max | default: 5
  assign m = product.metafields.custom
  assign ticks = ''

  # 1. Which dog it takes. Prefer the metafield; otherwise read the weight out of
  # the title, which is written "... for Dogs up to 70kg" across the range.
  assign weight = m.max_dog_weight.value | default: ''
  if weight == blank and product.title contains 'up to '
    assign tail = product.title | split: 'up to ' | last
    if tail contains 'kg'
      assign weight = tail | split: 'kg' | first | append: 'kg'
    endif
  endif
  if weight != blank
    assign ticks = ticks | append: 'Fits dogs up to ' | append: weight | append: '|'
  endif

  # 2. What is inside it. Only beds that actually have a core get this line:
  # core_type also carries values like "Mesh" on the elevated cots, and "Mesh core"
  # would describe a bed that has no core at all. Depth joins only when the store
  # knows it, and an approximate depth ("About 10cm") is lowercased so the line
  # reads as a sentence rather than two fragments.
  assign core = m.core_type.value | default: ''
  if core != blank and core contains 'oam'
    assign core_line = core | append: ' core'
    assign depth = m.foam_depth.value | default: ''
    if depth != blank
      assign d1 = depth | slice: 0 | downcase
      assign drest = depth | slice: 1, 40
      assign core_line = core_line | append: ', ' | append: d1 | append: drest | append: ' deep'
    endif
    assign ticks = ticks | append: core_line | append: '|'
  endif

  # 3. The cover. The metafield holds a short noun ("Zip-off fabric", "Coated,
  # wipe clean"), which reads like a spec sheet on its own, so give the two
  # common kinds their plain-English line and let anything else fall back.
  assign cover = m.cover_type.value | default: ''
  if cover != blank
    assign cover_l = cover | downcase
    if cover_l contains 'wipe' or cover_l contains 'coated'
      assign cover_line = 'Wipe-clean cover'
    elsif cover_l contains 'zip'
      assign cover_line = 'Zip-off cover for washing'
    else
      assign cover_line = cover | append: ' cover'
    endif
    assign ticks = ticks | append: cover_line | append: '|'
  endif

  # 4. Getting in. Only a low front earns a line: the shape is already obvious
  # from the title and the photographs, and "Nest shape" as a tick says nothing.
  if m.low_entry.value == true
    assign ticks = ticks | append: 'Low step-in front|'
  endif

  # 5. How long it is backed, only for beds the guarantee actually covers.
  if m.foam_guarantee.value == true and settings.pln_guarantee_enable
    assign years = settings.pln_guarantee_years | default: 5
    assign ticks = ticks | append: years | append: '-year foam guarantee|'
  endif

  assign ticks = ticks | split: '|'
-%}
{%- if ticks.size > 0 -%}
  {{ 'pln-pdp.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <ul class="pln-spec-ticks" aria-label="What this bed is">
    {%- for tick in ticks limit: limit -%}
      {%- if tick != blank -%}
        <li>{% render 'pln-icon', name: 'check', class: 'pln-icon--success' %}<span>{{ tick }}</span></li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
{%- endif -%}
